  "phase4": {
    "status": "deferred \u2014 user-approved no-force; no prompt wording changed",
    "principle": "Low overlap between a variant and the core is NOT a defect. Share genuine common policy only. Where a variant's wording encodes a runtime contract, transport protocol, or UI requirement, that text stays in the adapter and is NOT generalized into core. A shared policy is applied only after behavioral evals show it does not contradict that contract.",
    "deferred": [
      {
        "target": "prompts/adapters/gpt-astra.md",
        "ref": "gpt-astra.txt:46",
        "contract": "Do not spawn subagents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for subagents, delegation, or parallel agent work.",
        "conflictsWith": [
          "D29"
        ],
        "decision": "KEEP the scoped no-subagent rule. D29's search-routing guidance is shared only as a CONDITIONAL on the Task tool being available and permitted for this agent; where it is not, the variant routes through its own scoped path.",
        "action": "deferred to behavioral evals"
      },
      {
        "target": "prompts/adapters/beast.md",
        "ref": "beast.txt:20",
        "contract": "Always tell the user what you are going to do before making a tool call with a single concise sentence.",
        "conflictsWith": [
          "D31"
        ],
        "decision": "NARROW to consequential actions only. Pre-announce before an action that changes the user's system, spends meaningful time, or is not obvious; do not pre-announce routine reads and searches. D31's no-step-by-step-narration still governs the rest.",
        "action": "deferred to behavioral evals"
      },
      {
        "target": "prompts/adapters/beast.md",
        "ref": "beast.txt:76,142",
        "contract": "Todo lists must be written in markdown format, wrapped in triple backticks, and the updated list is displayed to the user on each checkoff.",
        "conflictsWith": [
          "D22"
        ],
        "decision": "STANDARDIZE BEHAVIOR FIRST: D22's phase-boundary batching cadence becomes the shared behavior (this is the part worth adopting fleet-wide). PRESENTATION is retained wherever the interface requires it \u2014 the fenced markdown rendering and per-checkoff display stay adapter-local rather than moving to core.",
        "action": "deferred to behavioral evals"
      },
      {
        "target": "prompts/adapters/gpt.md, prompts/adapters/meta.md",
        "ref": "gpt.txt:6; meta.txt:1",
        "contract": "gpt.txt:6 pins the `multi_tool_use.parallel` tool-parallelism protocol and the commentary/final channel contract; meta.txt:1 carries the `{{MODEL_NAME}}` template placeholder.",
        "conflictsWith": [
          "D30"
        ],
        "decision": "PRESERVE BOTH IN ADAPTERS. Protocol and template placeholders are transport/identity concerns, never shared policy. D30's shared parallelism rule may reference them but must not restate or override them; a core block may not contain a protocol name or template var.",
        "action": "deferred to behavioral evals"
      }
    ],
